     </draw:image>
    </draw:frame> utilized to make foods that could be a step towards curbing malnutrition. The published literature gives the total scenario of the chemical constituents, nutritional content, potential uses, and pharmacological activities of the plant. The identification, isolation, and standardization of plant extracts may be considered for detailed studies which can be useful for the further development of the promising food products with health benefits and nutrients to cure different life style-related diseases as well as malnutrition.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P48"/>
   <text:p text:style-name="P49"><text:span text:style-name="T33">Cautions</text:span>:</text:p>
   <text:list text:style-name="L7">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P50">Avoid Moringa from India which may be GMO treated (non Organic) and inconsitent quality.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P50">Pregnant women should consult their doctor.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P50">Persons using medications for high blood pressure should not combine with <text:span text:style-name="T19">Moringa</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P47"/>
  </office:text>
 </office:body>
</office:document>